WEBVTT

00:45.020 --> 00:47.070
Hmm, very nice.

03:10.040 --> 03:16.840
~Ensemble Contest~<b></b>

03:21.810 --> 03:25.350
Oh, Kumiko, we're starting!

03:25.350 --> 03:27.520
Eh, it's time already?!

03:27.520 --> 03:29.230
We'll go ahead of you!

03:29.230 --> 03:31.730
Ah... Ahh! Wait for me!

03:32.190 --> 03:34.110
Karaoke sounds good then!

03:34.570 --> 03:35.700
Why are you so late?

03:35.700 --> 03:37.950
Sorry, I was practicing.

03:37.950 --> 03:39.280
Oh.

03:39.280 --> 03:41.370
Hurry up...

03:41.950 --> 03:43.950
Music Room

03:48.500 --> 03:51.540
Attention everyone!

03:52.090 --> 03:54.090
And after that—

04:00.300 --> 04:02.140
Ugh...

04:04.890 --> 04:05.600
Kumiko.

04:05.600 --> 04:06.350
Oh...

04:07.600 --> 04:09.440
Yes...

04:11.650 --> 04:15.110
Okay then, let's begin the meeting.

04:15.110 --> 04:18.820
Firstly, please take a look at the sheet that was handed out earlier.

04:18.820 --> 04:20.570
Now that the cultural festival is over,

04:20.570 --> 04:26.250
today we're going to discuss the ensemble contest taking place in December.

04:26.830 --> 04:30.170
Umm... So... I'll hand it over to the drum major.

04:33.960 --> 04:40.550
The ensemble contest we will be participating in is similar to the brass band competition.

04:40.550 --> 04:45.470
There are divisions for junior high school, high school, college, and a general division.

04:44.680 --> 04:49.190
National Competition

04:44.680 --> 04:49.190
Kansai Competition

04:45.470 --> 04:50.140
The system for advancing from the prefectural to national championships is the same.

04:50.140 --> 04:52.980
The one difference is...

04:52.980 --> 04:56.110
that the performances are done in small groups.

04:56.110 --> 04:59.530
A group consists of at least 3 and no more than 8 members.

04:58.780 --> 05:03.530
3 to 8 people

04:58.780 --> 05:03.530
5 min limit

04:59.530 --> 05:02.450
The performance must be no longer than five minutes.

05:02.450 --> 05:06.490
The prefectural event will take place at the end of December.

05:06.490 --> 05:11.290
In addition, there can only be one group that performs per school.

05:13.960 --> 05:17.460
Oh... and this is the important part.

05:17.460 --> 05:21.050
Taki-sensei wants more than just a few people involved.

05:21.050 --> 05:24.760
He wants everyone here to do something.

05:24.760 --> 05:27.390
What? You mean...

05:27.390 --> 05:28.390
Yes!

05:30.890 --> 05:36.110
Each of you is free to organize your own group according to your own discretion.

05:36.110 --> 05:41.570
In early December, we will hold a concert and audition.

05:41.570 --> 05:44.200
And...

05:44.200 --> 05:48.870
That is how representatives who will participate in the Prefectural Tournament will be chosen!

05:48.870 --> 05:52.750
<i>2nd year at Kitauji High School. Concert band club president.</i>

05:52.750 --> 05:54.000
Is she for real?

05:54.540 --> 05:56.380
<i>Kumiko Oumae.</i>

05:56.380 --> 05:57.750
<i>Awkwardly in action.</i>

05:59.460 --> 06:03.470
Special OVA

05:59.460 --> 06:03.470
Ensemble Contest

06:04.840 --> 06:08.310
Ugh... Why did I do that...

06:08.310 --> 06:10.810
You focus too much on trying to make appearances.

06:10.810 --> 06:13.560
Well, I was nervous.

06:13.560 --> 06:16.650
You still get nervous at every meeting?

06:16.650 --> 06:20.280
Hmm... I'm fine when I'm talking,

06:20.280 --> 06:22.490
but once I'm finished, I'm suddenly tired.

06:22.490 --> 06:24.820
Well, I guess we'll just have to take it slow with you.

06:24.820 --> 06:26.160
Well you sure talk big.

06:26.160 --> 06:26.990
For real...

06:26.990 --> 06:29.790
I don't need a vice president to tell me that.

06:29.790 --> 06:31.450
Hey, hey...

06:31.450 --> 06:34.790
But about EnCon, we're cutting it a bit late, aren't we?

06:34.790 --> 06:36.710
Indeed...

06:37.500 --> 06:40.880
So... Kumiko, are you planning to team up with anyone?

06:40.880 --> 06:42.760
No, not yet.

06:43.260 --> 06:47.890
I might end up just joining with whoever is left out.

06:48.300 --> 06:49.470
I see.

06:50.720 --> 06:52.520
What about you, Reina?

06:52.730 --> 06:55.100
I don't have anyone either.

06:56.350 --> 06:57.270
It's just...

06:58.900 --> 07:02.530
I don't want to work with people who won't put in the effort.

07:02.530 --> 07:04.450
Oh... as expected.

07:04.450 --> 07:05.990
That's just like her...

07:05.990 --> 07:08.870
Staff
Room

07:07.280 --> 07:08.870
Excuse us.

07:08.870 --> 07:11.700
Oh, sorry for calling you guys.

07:11.700 --> 07:13.200
No problem.

07:13.620 --> 07:16.670
Sensei, I'm not sure, but your appearance seems a bit...

07:16.670 --> 07:20.840
Ah, maybe it's because I overslept.

07:20.840 --> 07:22.800
It's been pretty cold lately, so it just happened.

07:22.800 --> 07:24.420
That's right!

07:24.420 --> 07:28.010
I couldn't get out of my futon at all either.

07:28.010 --> 07:31.180
Oh, you too?

07:31.180 --> 07:34.100
<i>Don't look, don't look, don't look, don't look!</i>

07:34.100 --> 07:37.060
So, why did you call us?

07:37.060 --> 07:41.770
Yes, I'd like to discuss something related to the audition.

07:41.770 --> 07:43.280
A discussion?

07:43.280 --> 07:44.320
Yes.

07:44.320 --> 07:50.530
This time, I'd like to have students vote for the auditions, instead of just me or Matsumoto-sensei.

07:50.530 --> 07:52.660
What? Really?

07:52.660 --> 07:54.200
Yes.

07:54.200 --> 07:59.040
It is very important to evaluate the performances objectively.

07:59.040 --> 08:01.880
Which is why I think it's a good idea.

08:01.880 --> 08:07.630
Though I wasn't sure if I should have the third-year students also participate in voting.

08:07.630 --> 08:09.890
Third year students, huh?

08:09.890 --> 08:15.020
Well, it's a concert, and I'm sure some seniors will be there to watch.

08:15.020 --> 08:18.520
I think it'd be better if they do participate.

08:18.520 --> 08:22.060
I think they can look at it objectively, since they aren't directly involved.

08:22.060 --> 08:24.190
I disagree.

08:24.190 --> 08:29.280
I think having only the performance members vote would be enough.

08:30.240 --> 08:31.410
I see.

08:32.410 --> 08:35.750
Now that the Vice President and the Drum Major have given their thoughts,

08:36.370 --> 08:37.710
What do you think President?

08:37.710 --> 08:38.290
Uh...

08:38.710 --> 08:39.830
Well... you see...

08:40.920 --> 08:43.710
So... Uhm...

08:44.710 --> 08:47.840
Uhh...

08:48.380 --> 08:52.800
Well... maybe we could split the vote into two.

08:53.260 --> 08:55.350
A vote by the current students,

08:55.350 --> 09:01.400
and a public vote by the guests, including third years, who come to see the concert...

09:01.400 --> 09:02.310
Hmm...

09:02.310 --> 09:03.230
That might work!

09:03.230 --> 09:04.020
Eh?

09:04.020 --> 09:05.820
Yes, it might.

09:05.820 --> 09:10.530
But then there is a possibility that the results will be divided.

09:10.530 --> 09:11.660
Right...?

09:11.660 --> 09:14.280
If it comes to that, then I think we should take Kousaka's advice.

09:14.280 --> 09:18.200
I think it's a good idea to prioritize the votes of the current student body.

09:18.200 --> 09:19.290
I see.

09:20.120 --> 09:22.120
Kousaka, what do you think?

09:22.460 --> 09:24.750
I wouldn't mind it.

09:25.630 --> 09:27.340
Okay, understood.

09:27.630 --> 09:32.380
Alright, let's have separate voting for the students and the public.

09:32.380 --> 09:34.010
What? Are you sure?

09:34.350 --> 09:38.560
Yes, I think it would work.

09:38.890 --> 09:42.650
Distributing the decision among many individuals, I think it's an excellent idea.

09:43.940 --> 09:46.860
It seems we've agreed to do that...

09:46.860 --> 09:48.150
Hmm...

09:48.150 --> 09:51.150
However, I have to make sure to explain it properly in advance.

09:51.150 --> 09:53.200
Otherwise it might cause complaints later.

09:53.200 --> 09:54.910
What might cause complaints?

09:56.080 --> 09:57.910
No, it's nothing.

09:57.910 --> 09:59.410
Prez?!

09:59.410 --> 10:01.460
Are you here?

10:01.460 --> 10:03.540
I've come to give you a list of our group members.

10:03.540 --> 10:05.210
Huh?! You've decided already?

10:05.210 --> 10:06.250
Please!

10:05.750 --> 10:06.670
Woodwind quintet

10:06.250 --> 10:07.380
Woah, fancy!

10:07.380 --> 10:08.460
Heh...?

10:08.460 --> 10:11.260
Oh, you didn't team up with Kanade?

10:11.550 --> 10:14.260
I wanted to partner up with her...

10:14.260 --> 10:16.890
But Kanade is in the brass section and I'm a woodwin—

10:16.890 --> 10:19.640
She's trying to cover it up.

10:19.640 --> 10:23.020
This little one said their group is doing a woodwind quintet.

10:23.020 --> 10:25.600
Oh, Kanade told you before I could.

10:26.690 --> 10:28.980
Well then, what about you, Kanade?

10:28.980 --> 10:31.150
Our little one here also took the horn player.

10:31.150 --> 10:32.650
Ah...?

10:32.650 --> 10:37.200
Because a woodwind quintet needs a horn.

10:37.200 --> 10:39.700
I'm sorry for being so cute.

10:39.700 --> 10:41.120
Please ignore her.

10:41.120 --> 10:41.500
Wha-

10:41.500 --> 10:42.160
So mean!

10:42.160 --> 10:43.750
Being cute has nothing to do with it.

10:42.160 --> 10:43.710
Woah...

10:43.750 --> 10:46.250
Everyone is getting more and more serious about this...

10:46.250 --> 10:48.380
It's because we have limited instruments.

10:48.710 --> 10:52.050
If you have someone you want, it's better to act quickly.

10:52.050 --> 10:54.220
Ah, that's right...

10:54.220 --> 10:57.260
Ueh... Did someone already ask you to join?

10:57.800 --> 10:58.970
"No comment".

10:58.970 --> 11:00.260
That's a 'yes', isn't it?

11:00.680 --> 11:02.060
Eh!

11:02.060 --> 11:05.980
You said you were going to play a baritone quartet with me...

11:05.980 --> 11:08.560
When did you ever ask me?

11:08.810 --> 11:10.690
I asked through telekinesis!

11:09.610 --> 11:10.690
That's not possible.

11:11.280 --> 11:12.530
Horn Trio

11:11.570 --> 11:12.530
Here you go.

11:12.530 --> 11:13.570
Thanks.

11:13.570 --> 11:14.950
One group after another.

11:15.400 --> 11:17.240
A French horn trio?

11:17.240 --> 11:17.910
Huh?

11:17.910 --> 11:22.040
Yes, I was thinking of doing Reicha's 'Six Trios'.

11:22.040 --> 11:23.370
I see.

11:23.370 --> 11:26.330
President, are you going to be partnering with Kousaka?

11:26.330 --> 11:28.540
Ahh. Eh?

11:28.920 --> 11:32.050
No, we haven't decided yet. Why?

11:32.050 --> 11:34.670
Ah... Oh. I see.

11:34.670 --> 11:38.970
Just now, Kousaka invited our part leader to join her group, so I assumed...

11:38.970 --> 11:41.180
Oh, I see. Is that so?

11:41.180 --> 11:45.390
Uhm... Sorry then, I'll excuse myself now.

11:45.390 --> 11:46.310
Mm-hmm.

11:47.560 --> 11:51.730
Are you perhaps feeling a little left out?

11:51.730 --> 11:54.320
It's Reina. She has her own reasons.

11:55.530 --> 11:57.070
That's true.

11:57.070 --> 11:58.030
What?

11:59.490 --> 12:02.280
<i>As the ensemble contest draws closer,</i>

12:02.280 --> 12:04.620
<i>things get busy with the band</i>.

12:05.370 --> 12:07.790
<i>There's less than two months left.</i>

12:07.790 --> 12:11.420
<i>The audition to decide the representatives will be held in early December.</i>

12:12.170 --> 12:16.800
<i>Considering the time it takes to form a team, choose a piece, and practice,</i>

12:16.800 --> 12:20.090
<i>the schedule becomes quite tight.</i>

12:23.140 --> 12:24.060
Mmm.

12:25.020 --> 12:26.060
Yes!

12:36.190 --> 12:40.360
My duties as the president and my own practice time.

12:40.990 --> 12:43.660
It's okay for now.

12:44.790 --> 12:47.000
Haa...

12:48.870 --> 12:53.170
Ahhh... but when I think about the upcoming contest...

12:54.960 --> 12:56.670
Are you crying?

12:56.670 --> 12:57.670
Huh?

12:59.590 --> 13:00.970
Hmm?

13:00.970 --> 13:04.970
Uhm... uhm...

13:06.930 --> 13:09.600
Uhh... or... not?

13:12.650 --> 13:15.690
Agh! Ahh! Oh!

13:15.690 --> 13:18.570
Don't be so scared... it's me.

13:18.570 --> 13:20.200
Huh? Oh.

13:20.900 --> 13:24.240
Yoroizuka... senpai?

13:26.620 --> 13:27.870
Yes.

13:31.920 --> 13:34.040
What are you doing here?

13:34.040 --> 13:35.540
Were you crying?

13:35.540 --> 13:37.920
Oh, no I wasn't.

13:37.920 --> 13:40.220
What made you think so?

13:40.760 --> 13:42.430
Just a hunch.

13:42.430 --> 13:45.050
Are you practicing here?

13:45.050 --> 13:49.810
Yeah, Taki-sensei arranged an empty classroom for me.

13:49.810 --> 13:51.980
You're preparing for music college entrance exams, right?

13:51.980 --> 13:52.940
Yes.

13:52.940 --> 13:56.730
Oh right. Ririka is doing her best as a part leader.

13:59.070 --> 14:00.990
That's good to hear.

14:04.700 --> 14:07.450
You're going to get your fingers dirty.

14:07.450 --> 14:08.080
Yes...

14:08.080 --> 14:10.330
What do you mean "yes"?

14:11.500 --> 14:13.210
You're good at opening the window.

14:13.210 --> 14:14.710
Eh?

14:14.710 --> 14:17.460
It was stuck earlier so...

14:17.460 --> 14:22.090
Oh, it might be tricky from the inside.

14:22.090 --> 14:23.630
That's not it.

14:25.510 --> 14:30.270
It's good that you know what you're doing.

14:30.270 --> 14:34.230
Ehh? I don't really get what you mean.

14:35.900 --> 14:38.730
You're skilled at opening the window.

14:39.190 --> 14:40.610
That's all.

14:40.610 --> 14:42.360
Hm? Okay.

14:44.110 --> 14:45.490
EnCon Teams

14:46.570 --> 14:49.910
The posters have really been piling up here these past few days.

14:50.450 --> 14:52.700
Oumae Kumiko

14:56.580 --> 14:57.750
Prez!

14:59.210 --> 15:00.800
Kumiko-senpai!

15:00.800 --> 15:01.340
Oh!

15:02.050 --> 15:03.050
Here you go.

15:02.050 --> 15:03.920
Brass Sextet

15:03.170 --> 15:05.630
Ah! So it's been decided, huh?

15:05.630 --> 15:07.180
That's right!

15:07.180 --> 15:10.220
The trombonist asked me to work together!

15:10.220 --> 15:12.600
That's great!

15:12.600 --> 15:14.560
Kanade and Micchan have also decided.

15:14.560 --> 15:15.520
Mhm.

15:15.520 --> 15:18.480
Looks like they have seven members. A brass septuplet.

15:18.480 --> 15:24.570
Brass
Septet

15:19.060 --> 15:20.730
I wonder what they're going to play?

15:20.730 --> 15:23.900
I think they said their playing "Tea Time".

15:23.900 --> 15:26.160
This group is pretty stacked, huh?

15:26.160 --> 15:29.660
With so many skilled members, I'm looking forward to their performance.

15:32.330 --> 15:34.330
What are you guys going to play?

15:34.330 --> 15:41.500
EnCon Teams

15:34.750 --> 15:38.670
We're gonna play Richard's "Homage to the Noble Grape"!

15:38.670 --> 15:41.500
That's a song for 10 players, isn't it?

15:41.500 --> 15:42.670
Yup!

15:42.670 --> 15:46.880
It won't be impossible to play if we work hard arranging it though.

15:47.300 --> 15:50.970
I feel like I'd slack off if we did something too simple.

15:50.970 --> 15:52.010
Heh heh heh...

15:52.760 --> 15:53.720
Good girl!

15:53.720 --> 15:55.140
Huh?

15:55.140 --> 15:57.310
I-is that right?

15:57.310 --> 15:58.810
Yup. Very good.

16:00.690 --> 16:04.990
<i>The ability to not harbor envy
in the face of someone better.</i>

16:04.990 --> 16:08.070
<i>I'm not sure if it's a virtue or a flaw.</i>

16:08.410 --> 16:10.200
<i>What should I tell her?</i>

16:10.200 --> 16:15.000
<i>It's times like these where I
question what to do as president.</i>

16:15.620 --> 16:19.370
<i>Right then, an uncomfortable ache began to solidify in me.</i>

16:19.370 --> 16:23.340
<i>I have to keep in mind that I'm still inexperienced.</i>

16:25.300 --> 16:26.880
Still a long way to go.

16:26.880 --> 16:28.840
Thanks for the hard work.

16:28.840 --> 16:30.090
Good work!

16:31.220 --> 16:32.510
Sorry I'm so late!

16:32.890 --> 16:35.270
It's okay. It's part of the job.

16:35.270 --> 16:37.060
That's right.

16:37.060 --> 16:39.940
I don't think you should apologize about it.

16:39.940 --> 16:40.850
Oh.

16:41.230 --> 16:46.110
In that case, what do you have to say, Miss?

16:46.110 --> 16:48.900
Yes, Kawashima-sensei!

16:47.570 --> 16:48.900
Something new between them, huh?

16:48.900 --> 16:51.030
Thank you very much.

16:51.030 --> 16:52.280
You're welcome.

16:53.910 --> 16:56.200
Since you're the club president Kumiko,

16:56.540 --> 17:01.210
Midori thinks it would be best to only apologize when it's necessary.

17:01.630 --> 17:05.670
Ah, that makes sense...

17:05.670 --> 17:10.340
If the president appears too meek, it can lower the morale of the members.

17:10.800 --> 17:13.050
It's so complicated.

17:13.050 --> 17:15.430
It's a hard job, huh? Being the president...

17:15.430 --> 17:18.100
It requires a lot of thinking.

17:19.100 --> 17:22.850
Kumiko, you can always rely on others.

17:22.850 --> 17:25.860
That's why you have a drum major and a vice president.

17:25.860 --> 17:28.820
That's right! We're here too!

17:28.820 --> 17:32.280
Exactly, feel free to tell us anything.

17:32.280 --> 17:33.820
Thanks everyone.

17:34.240 --> 17:37.080
In that case... how about treating me to some meat buns?

17:37.080 --> 17:40.040
Hold up, that's not what we meant!

17:42.750 --> 17:48.300
Oh yeah, has Suzuki the tuba player already joined a group?

17:48.300 --> 17:50.130
You mean Micchan?

17:50.130 --> 17:52.680
Yeah, Mirei already joined Kanade's group.

17:52.680 --> 17:55.930
Oh right, she did.

17:56.390 --> 17:58.020
Impressive move, Hisaishi.

17:58.020 --> 17:59.980
She's crafty, isn't she?

18:01.230 --> 18:04.900
Oh right, you've also been gathering a group, right Reina?

18:05.400 --> 18:07.610
I heard from a girl in the horn section.

18:07.610 --> 18:09.230
Yup.

18:10.150 --> 18:11.320
I see...

18:11.320 --> 18:12.450
So what?

18:12.450 --> 18:14.570
Ah. Nothing.

18:18.700 --> 18:21.410
Ahhh, my Tubacabra...

18:22.000 --> 18:25.040
Its plating has started to peel.

18:25.040 --> 18:27.920
Your tuba isn't plated, the proper term is lacquer.

18:27.920 --> 18:28.920
Really?

18:29.300 --> 18:31.970
Well, at least I wasn't too far off the mark.

18:31.970 --> 18:35.720
It's like calling a steelhead trout a "trout salmon".

18:35.720 --> 18:38.720
Eh? What's the difference?

18:38.720 --> 18:40.930
While trout is a freshwater fish,

18:41.310 --> 18:45.940
steelhead trout is a breed of trout that can also live in the sea.

18:47.310 --> 18:48.770
Wow!

18:48.770 --> 18:51.690
Reina, are you a fish expert?

18:51.690 --> 18:54.860
I only know because my father loves fish.

18:55.950 --> 19:00.200
I have some shopping to do, see you later!

19:00.200 --> 19:02.910
Okay, see you later.

19:02.910 --> 19:04.540
See you tomorrow!

19:07.380 --> 19:10.920
Your dad likes fish a lot, huh?

19:11.380 --> 19:12.460
Mhm.

19:12.460 --> 19:15.630
There's lots one doesn't know, isn't there?

19:15.630 --> 19:19.760
I don't know anything about your father.

19:19.760 --> 19:22.850
Well, we don't talk about little things like that.

19:22.850 --> 19:24.520
Indeed we don't.

19:26.900 --> 19:30.940
Oh yeah Kumiko, why don't we form an ensemble together?

19:32.030 --> 19:34.650
I was thinking of doing a wind and percussion octet.

19:35.240 --> 19:37.910
I actually invited Katou earlier.

19:41.080 --> 19:43.370
What... why the face.

19:43.370 --> 19:47.370
Why? Well, the timing is a bit different than what I expected.

19:47.370 --> 19:48.880
I'm a bit pissed.

19:48.880 --> 19:50.920
What?

19:50.920 --> 19:52.380
You don't like the idea?

19:52.380 --> 19:55.470
Hmm... I'm thinking...

19:55.470 --> 19:57.130
Well I guess if you don't want to...

19:57.380 --> 19:58.300
Eh?! No!

19:58.300 --> 20:00.510
That was a lie! I want to! Please let me!

20:00.510 --> 20:01.600
What?

20:01.600 --> 20:03.770
Eh, well...

20:04.730 --> 20:07.350
<i>It was only a matter of time from there.</i>

20:07.350 --> 20:10.560
<i>People who Reina already approached included horn player Morimoto,</i>

20:10.560 --> 20:14.070
<i>Inoue the percussionist,</i>

20:14.070 --> 20:17.490
<i>trumpet player Kohinata,</i>

20:17.490 --> 20:18.450
<i>and also...</i>

20:18.450 --> 20:20.700
<i>another percussionist, Kamaya.</i>

20:20.700 --> 20:26.620
<i>Though, she had been declining because she thought she wasn't good enough.</i>

20:26.620 --> 20:30.580
Her and I were comrades on Team Monaka. Leave convincing her to me!

20:34.170 --> 20:36.880
Well, if you push for it so strongly, Hazuki...

20:37.550 --> 20:40.220
Yeah, then it would be rude to decline.

20:40.930 --> 20:42.390
Wow!

20:42.390 --> 20:42.970
Really?

20:42.970 --> 20:44.390
Y-yes.

20:46.310 --> 20:47.770
Okay...

20:48.310 --> 20:49.690
A key?

20:49.690 --> 20:51.690
She said okay.

20:52.860 --> 20:55.280
<i>And so, we finished gathering all the members.</i>

20:55.280 --> 20:56.610
Culinary Room

20:56.610 --> 20:57.780
Well..

20:57.780 --> 21:00.820
It feels a bit weird to be introducing myself so formally.

20:58.530 --> 21:03.580
Trombone, 2nd year
Shuuichi Tsukamoto

21:00.950 --> 21:03.580
I'm the trombone player, Shuuichi Tsukamoto.

21:04.410 --> 21:06.160
What's with that reaction?

21:06.790 --> 21:10.500
I didn't tell you? I think he's a capable player, isn't he?

21:10.500 --> 21:11.790
Oh reeally?

21:11.170 --> 21:11.790
Oi...

21:11.790 --> 21:13.750
I-I'm a trumpet player.

21:11.790 --> 21:16.710
Trumpet, 1st year
Yume Kohinata

21:13.750 --> 21:15.590
Yume Kohinata.

21:15.590 --> 21:18.050
As the only first year here, it's a bit awkward.

21:18.050 --> 21:21.680
Now now, no need to be worried.

21:21.680 --> 21:23.800
Ah... thank you.

21:23.800 --> 21:27.560
I'm Junna Inoue from the percussion section. I'm looking forward to working with you.

21:23.800 --> 21:27.560
Percussion, 2nd year
Junna Inoue

21:27.560 --> 21:32.560
I'm Tsubame Kamaya, also a second-year percussion student.
Nice to meet you.

21:27.560 --> 21:32.560
Percussion, 2nd year
Tsubame Kamaya

21:32.560 --> 21:36.570
Tuba! I'm Hazuki Katou.
I'll do my best!

21:32.560 --> 21:36.570
Tuba, 2nd year
Hazuki Katou

21:36.570 --> 21:39.070
Michiyo Morimoto. I play horn.

21:36.570 --> 21:41.610
Horn, 2nd year
Michiyo Morimoto

21:39.070 --> 21:43.070
Actually, I'm nervous too, being surrounded by all these executives.

21:43.070 --> 21:44.950
Don't be, we're in the same year.

21:44.950 --> 21:46.990
Well yeah, but...

21:46.990 --> 21:48.250
I understand how you feel!

21:48.250 --> 21:49.080
Right?

21:49.080 --> 21:50.080
Eh?

21:50.080 --> 21:53.790
Uhm, I'm euphonium player Kumiko Oumae.

21:50.080 --> 21:55.590
Euphonium, 2nd year
Kumiko Oumae

21:53.920 --> 21:55.590
I look forward to working with everyone.

21:55.590 --> 22:00.470
Trumpet, 2nd year
Reina Kousaka

21:55.880 --> 21:59.510
Reina Kousaka, in charge of trumpet.

21:59.510 --> 22:00.470
Nice to meet you.

22:00.470 --> 22:02.630
I'm starting to get excited!

22:02.630 --> 22:04.340
We're gonna be busy starting now, right?

22:04.340 --> 22:05.470
Yup!

22:05.470 --> 22:06.890
When I commit to something,

22:06.890 --> 22:09.310
I want to try my hardest to not have any regrets.

22:09.310 --> 22:12.190
Let's stay focused and give it our all.

22:12.190 --> 22:13.900
Yes, yes! Of course!

22:15.110 --> 22:23.860
Brass & Percussion Octet

22:15.110 --> 22:23.860
Aim for first!

22:15.110 --> 22:23.860
Full ensemble!

22:15.110 --> 22:23.860
Let's do it!!

22:16.570 --> 22:19.440
<i>And thus, our brass & percussion ensemble was officially formed</i>

22:19.440 --> 22:23.860
<i>so we could participate in our school's preliminary audition!</i>

22:37.040 --> 22:39.250
Prez, what should we do?

22:39.250 --> 22:41.380
Our members haven't been decided.

22:41.670 --> 22:44.090
Oh... lets see...

22:44.090 --> 22:45.680
I'm sorry.

22:45.680 --> 22:48.560
No, no. No need to apologize.

22:48.560 --> 22:49.930
Just a moment.

22:49.930 --> 22:51.930
Umm...

22:52.770 --> 22:55.520
The only ones left are two contrabasses,

22:55.900 --> 23:00.030
four clarinets, and another one here... and here.

23:00.610 --> 23:03.990
With this many, we can probably put something together.

23:03.990 --> 23:05.410
I think you're right...

23:05.860 --> 23:10.580
I'll think about it a bit as well. Let me know if you make any progress.

23:11.040 --> 23:13.040
Thank you!

23:13.040 --> 23:15.330
You're very kind, Prez.

23:20.840 --> 23:22.590
So my only strength is that I'm nice?!

23:24.590 --> 23:27.680
No, I'm not just trying to be kind, but as the president—

23:27.680 --> 23:28.680
Woah!

23:28.680 --> 23:31.220
Oh! I came at just the right time.

23:31.220 --> 23:32.810
Here's the sheet.

23:31.220 --> 23:32.810
Contrabass Duet

23:33.600 --> 23:35.810
Contrabass duet?

23:35.810 --> 23:39.520
No one asked me to join, so in that case...

23:39.520 --> 23:43.570
I thought I could just form a duet with Motomu, and teach him some things...

23:43.570 --> 23:46.610
It might help him level up.

23:47.200 --> 23:48.740
What piece are you planning to play?

23:48.740 --> 23:52.200
I'm thinking about Beethoven's Minuet.

23:52.200 --> 23:56.670
Oh, speaking of which, the clarinets were talking about doing a quartet.

23:56.670 --> 23:57.540
Eh?!

23:57.540 --> 23:59.710
This worsens the situation!

24:00.710 --> 24:02.050
Indeed...

24:02.050 --> 24:03.340
So that means...

24:03.880 --> 24:06.760
We would have four fewer people than from the list.

24:06.760 --> 24:07.800
Not good.

24:08.760 --> 24:10.680
It was inevitable, wasn't it?

24:10.680 --> 24:15.100
There's no way everyone in the club would be perfectly assigned.

24:15.560 --> 24:19.190
But we have to do something about those that are left.

24:19.730 --> 24:21.440
Maybe we could gather a few from other groups

24:21.440 --> 24:25.530
and ask them to participate in two performances or something.

24:25.530 --> 24:26.990
I don't think we should do that.

24:26.990 --> 24:30.620
It would overburden those individuals and cause the performances to suffer.

24:32.450 --> 24:35.790
I understand that, but...

24:35.790 --> 24:38.460
It's not possible, you know.

24:38.460 --> 24:41.250
But Tsubame, I thought you couldn't do kicks.

24:41.250 --> 24:43.420
Can you move your hands and feet separately?

24:43.920 --> 24:45.260
Well...

24:45.670 --> 24:49.260
The marimba is very important in the piece we're playing.

24:49.260 --> 24:52.050
I think you and the marimba go well together.

24:52.430 --> 24:53.390
What?

24:53.390 --> 24:55.470
Kamaya seems reluctant to play marimba.

24:55.970 --> 24:59.390
You heard how the timing was off when we rehearsed earlier, right?

24:59.390 --> 25:00.770
Yeah...

25:00.770 --> 25:04.190
Right now, the tuba and marimba are the only areas that need improvement.

25:05.030 --> 25:08.030
I had high hopes for the tuba, but...

25:10.200 --> 25:12.320
Let's resume in 10 minutes?

25:12.320 --> 25:14.490
Okay, got it. Sounds good.

25:15.870 --> 25:19.500
But wasn't it you who suggested Tsubame, Reina?

25:19.500 --> 25:20.870
Well, yes...

25:21.540 --> 25:22.750
Cause she's skilled.

25:23.210 --> 25:24.750
Then what about Shuuichi?

25:25.000 --> 25:27.260
Same. Because he's a good player.

25:28.130 --> 25:29.760
What? Are you doubting me?

25:30.800 --> 25:34.800
As for Kohinata, she was the one who asked me, not the other way around.

25:34.800 --> 25:36.260
Eh? Really?

25:36.560 --> 25:42.480
Yeah, after resolving to aim for EnCon, she came to me herself.

25:42.940 --> 25:46.480
It's very brave of her as a junior to invite a senior.

25:46.820 --> 25:48.490
Especially someone like you.

25:48.940 --> 25:52.610
There was a piece she had been wanting to play since middle school.

25:53.240 --> 25:55.490
That's why she asked to perform it together.

25:55.870 --> 25:59.500
And, she's talented as well.

26:00.870 --> 26:03.750
So I guess you prioritize everyone's skill, huh?

26:04.080 --> 26:05.340
Well...

26:06.130 --> 26:08.880
Katou has improved a lot,

26:08.880 --> 26:12.220
And others like Suzuki rejected me as well.

26:12.840 --> 26:14.180
What about me?

26:14.760 --> 26:18.260
Did you invite me because Kanade turned you down?

26:18.720 --> 26:20.020
Would that bother you?

26:21.270 --> 26:23.440
It wouldn't really...

26:26.060 --> 26:27.900
Actually, it would.

26:27.900 --> 26:28.940
Why?

26:29.650 --> 26:34.820
Because if Reina's the one choosing...

26:35.240 --> 26:38.950
then I want to be first pick.

26:41.540 --> 26:45.790
To be honest, Hisaishi was never invited.

26:45.790 --> 26:48.630
Out of the euphs, you were my top preference.

26:49.340 --> 26:52.130
Why did you invite me so late then?

26:53.510 --> 26:57.550
That's because I knew you wouldn't team up with anybody but me.

26:57.550 --> 26:59.760
Eh? You're lying.

27:00.520 --> 27:04.350
When I asked earlier, you said you would just go with the flow.

27:04.350 --> 27:08.860
And in middle school, you were always chosen right away.

27:09.570 --> 27:10.440
So...

27:16.110 --> 27:18.950
I couldn't handle the thought of you rejecting me.

27:22.450 --> 27:26.000
I had been wanting to do it together with you.

27:26.000 --> 27:27.920
Thanks so much for inviting me!

27:28.920 --> 27:31.800
It's nothing to thank me for.

27:32.840 --> 27:36.430
I've been saying for a while now. That you're the best euphonium player...

27:36.430 --> 27:38.720
Yes, yes. I'm very happy about it all.

27:38.720 --> 27:40.050
Get off me.

27:40.050 --> 27:42.430
Ow... haha.

27:50.820 --> 27:51.940
Stop that...

27:56.490 --> 28:00.950
<i>If someone better than me joins next year...</i>

28:00.950 --> 28:02.830
<i>I wonder who Reina would choose?</i>

28:04.040 --> 28:07.080
<i>The question grazed my mind for a fleeting instant,</i>

28:07.080 --> 28:08.880
<i>before I quickly suppressed the thought.</i>

28:11.170 --> 28:12.710
Um...

28:13.090 --> 28:14.710
Why are you guys here?

28:14.710 --> 28:16.300
Why?

28:16.300 --> 28:19.590
Cause we're worried about the new prez of course!

28:20.090 --> 28:22.510
You seem quite upbeat despite that.

28:23.140 --> 28:26.350
Actually, it's cause we heard the concert will also be an audition,

28:26.350 --> 28:29.150
for picking the representatives for EnCon.

28:29.150 --> 28:31.270
Yes... Wait, what?

28:31.270 --> 28:34.440
I was wondering if we could be of some help.

28:34.780 --> 28:37.070
We do have some time now after all.

28:37.070 --> 28:39.950
Eh? But... your exams...

28:39.950 --> 28:43.200
It's over. All three of us passed.

28:43.200 --> 28:44.410
Really?!

28:44.990 --> 28:48.870
Actually, there are a few who haven't joined a group yet.

28:48.870 --> 28:51.290
If it's okay with you, maybe you could help support them...

28:51.580 --> 28:52.540
Ugh!

28:52.540 --> 28:55.760
Before that, isn't there something you should say?

28:55.760 --> 28:58.010
Ah.

28:58.010 --> 28:59.720
I offer my congratulations.

28:59.720 --> 29:00.010
Mm.

29:01.720 --> 29:02.970
3rd year

29:01.720 --> 29:02.970
Yuuko Yoshikawa

29:01.720 --> 29:02.970
Nozomi Kasaki

29:01.720 --> 29:02.970
Natsuki Nakagawa

29:02.970 --> 29:04.220
Well then...

29:04.220 --> 29:05.770
Let us know once it's decided!

29:05.770 --> 29:07.310
Thanks guys.

29:07.310 --> 29:09.140
Appreciate the work, Prez!

29:10.190 --> 29:13.980
They even wrote down Natsuki's name without telling her...

29:13.980 --> 29:17.740
Midori heard she was also accepted into the same school.

29:18.110 --> 29:20.610
I should confirm, just in case...

29:21.610 --> 29:22.620
And also...

29:22.620 --> 29:24.240
No, I'm not doing it.

29:24.660 --> 29:27.040
Of course, you have entrance exams.

29:27.040 --> 29:30.210
Sorry for asking so suddenly.

29:30.670 --> 29:33.960
No, I'm glad you asked.

29:34.540 --> 29:39.220
Can you thank Nozomi for me? Just tell her "thanks".

29:39.550 --> 29:43.220
I can... But shouldn't you say it yourself?

29:44.800 --> 29:46.970
But I did say it.

29:47.270 --> 29:49.020
Is that so?

29:49.020 --> 29:50.810
Yes.

29:53.270 --> 29:56.570
Should I... close the window?

29:59.610 --> 30:01.900
No. It's fine.

30:06.280 --> 30:07.830
Let's see...

30:09.370 --> 30:12.080
Hm? Oumae?

30:13.420 --> 30:15.750
Long time no see. What's up?

30:15.750 --> 30:19.170
Yuuko came to the music room yesterday.

30:19.170 --> 30:20.670
Have you heard anything?

30:20.970 --> 30:22.800
Huh? Nope.

30:23.800 --> 30:25.430
I knew it!

30:25.430 --> 30:27.560
Shouldn't we mention something else before that?

30:27.560 --> 30:28.510
Huh?

30:28.510 --> 30:32.060
An underclassman just now rolled up to your classroom all fancy-like.

30:32.060 --> 30:33.730
Fancy-like?

30:34.310 --> 30:35.690
Did anything change?

30:35.690 --> 30:37.770
Do you not notice?

30:38.190 --> 30:40.360
I got a haircut at a hair salon yesterday.

30:40.940 --> 30:42.360
Five millimeters.

30:42.360 --> 30:43.780
How would I notice that?!

30:43.780 --> 30:45.910
Take some juice dammit!

30:45.910 --> 30:48.830
President Kumiko! This is bullying! Bullying!

30:48.830 --> 30:52.790
Stop it you two, break time is almost over!

30:53.460 --> 30:54.710
Um...

30:54.710 --> 30:57.920
Why did you write my name down without permission?

30:57.920 --> 30:59.500
Let's answer this with style...

30:59.840 --> 31:03.670
"Ah Natsuki, your sentiment alone is sufficient."

31:03.670 --> 31:05.300
I wouldn't want to hear that.

31:06.090 --> 31:07.430
Saying things like that...

31:07.430 --> 31:10.720
Aren't you turning into an annoying OG?

31:10.720 --> 31:13.640
Oumae, don't be afraid to chastise this...

31:13.640 --> 31:15.980
an-noy-ing brat.

31:15.980 --> 31:17.230
Who?

31:17.230 --> 31:19.480
So... about your participation?

31:19.480 --> 31:22.690
I don't mind, but it would be nice to be separate from this brat.

31:22.690 --> 31:25.450
Huh? What did you say just now?

31:25.450 --> 31:27.200
Okay... nice.

31:27.200 --> 31:28.660
Kanade, let's go.

31:28.660 --> 31:30.120
Huh? Oh...

31:30.740 --> 31:32.620
Is it okay to just leave them?

31:32.620 --> 31:34.120
Yup. It's fine.

31:34.790 --> 31:37.790
<i>With the help of the third-year students,</i>

31:37.790 --> 31:41.210
<i>everyone was assigned to a group.</i>

31:41.670 --> 31:43.590
<i>Throughout the month of November,</i>

31:44.050 --> 31:49.470
<i>the members diligently practiced for the December concert.</i>

31:49.470 --> 31:53.140
Decided!

31:59.690 --> 32:01.650
I'm late again.

32:02.400 --> 32:04.030
Oh, Kumiko!

32:04.690 --> 32:08.780
Hazuki was looking for you! Practice is starting!

32:08.780 --> 32:10.160
I know.

32:10.160 --> 32:11.330
Sorry, I'm late!

32:11.330 --> 32:12.620
You're dragging!

32:13.450 --> 32:17.170
The marimba tends to rush while the tuba tends to drag.

32:17.170 --> 32:20.250
Also, tuba needs to play with more dynamics.

32:20.250 --> 32:22.960
Otherwise the accents become difficult to hear.

32:23.210 --> 32:24.300
Yes!

32:24.630 --> 32:25.970
Yes...

32:26.300 --> 32:28.720
Okay, let's play from the beginning.

32:33.720 --> 32:34.890
Sorry.

32:34.890 --> 32:38.520
Midori already told you not to apologize so much.

32:38.520 --> 32:40.400
Ah... that's right.

32:40.400 --> 32:41.610
Kumiko.

32:41.610 --> 32:42.360
Yes?

32:42.820 --> 32:44.940
We'll play according to your tempo.

32:45.780 --> 32:46.940
Got it.

33:14.060 --> 33:15.930
<i>It's been one month.</i>

33:16.850 --> 33:19.520
<i>Our main concerns were the tuba and the marimba.</i>

33:19.520 --> 33:22.980
<i>The situation continued to be a bit of a muddle.</i>

33:24.110 --> 33:28.360
<i>Hazuki had been progressing very slowly.</i>

33:28.950 --> 33:34.330
<i>As for Tsubame, it felt like her
confidence was dwindling by the day.</i>

33:40.250 --> 33:42.580
Kumiko, what do you think?

33:43.130 --> 33:46.250
Ah? Ah.

33:46.590 --> 33:47.920
Tsubame.

33:48.760 --> 33:49.760
Yes.

33:50.340 --> 33:53.510
Let's practice together the next day off.

34:03.310 --> 34:05.570
Sounds beautiful.

34:05.570 --> 34:08.280
It's Nozomi's playing.

34:08.280 --> 34:09.740
Kumiko!

34:10.240 --> 34:13.410
You're practicing with Tsubame later, right?

34:13.410 --> 34:15.240
Can I join you?

34:15.660 --> 34:17.290
Of course.

34:17.290 --> 34:18.830
Alright, later!

34:19.580 --> 34:22.250
Well then, I shall take my leave as well.

34:22.790 --> 34:24.500
I'm not gonna lose.

34:24.500 --> 34:29.380
I consider the seniors my main rivals.

34:30.800 --> 34:33.380
Should I practice with you guys too?

34:33.380 --> 34:37.390
Well, that wouldn't be any different than our regular practice.

34:37.930 --> 34:40.390
Am I being too strict?

34:40.850 --> 34:44.310
No, I think what you're doing is correct.

34:45.270 --> 34:49.940
But sometimes hearing the truth can make you feel cornered.

34:51.240 --> 34:54.860
I just thought that it might be good to change the approach a bit.

34:59.700 --> 35:01.250
Does it bother you?

35:01.540 --> 35:04.000
Not exactly, but...

35:04.540 --> 35:09.000
I think it's okay for you to be yourself, Reina.

35:29.150 --> 35:33.030
I've been holding the group back... haven't I.

35:33.320 --> 35:35.610
I don't think so.

35:35.610 --> 35:37.030
No, I have.

35:37.570 --> 35:39.990
I understand it best.

35:39.990 --> 35:44.710
Micchan was probably Kousaka's first choice.

36:00.720 --> 36:02.060
Hazuki.

36:02.470 --> 36:05.850
You might be dragging the tempo because you're listening too hard.

36:05.850 --> 36:07.230
What do you mean?

36:07.560 --> 36:09.770
Uhm... with wind instruments.

36:09.770 --> 36:13.190
You have to take the time it takes to breathe into account, right?

36:13.190 --> 36:15.860
Are you doing that?

36:17.780 --> 36:20.410
You pay attention to every little breath when you play?

36:20.410 --> 36:24.160
No, not really. I guess it's more like a feeling.

36:24.160 --> 36:26.870
I've been mindful of it since I started playing.

36:26.870 --> 36:31.500
There are times when the sound I picture and the sound I make are perfectly aligned.

36:31.500 --> 36:32.880
Oh.

36:33.250 --> 36:37.220
Come to think of it, Gotou-senpai told me

36:37.720 --> 36:40.640
to consider the importance of the basics.

36:41.100 --> 36:43.220
Well, no choice but to give it our best.

36:43.220 --> 36:46.100
I'm gonna work hard and train like a warrior.

36:46.310 --> 36:49.230
I'm sorry. Were you waiting?

36:49.230 --> 36:51.480
No, let's get started.

36:51.480 --> 36:55.480
Before that, could you please listen to Tsubame play once?

37:26.310 --> 37:27.390
Hah...

37:27.390 --> 37:29.440
Woah...

37:30.350 --> 37:31.770
What do you think?

37:31.770 --> 37:34.400
It was good, I was surprised.

37:34.400 --> 37:36.820
You're good at marimba,Tsubame.

37:36.820 --> 37:37.860
Right?

37:38.530 --> 37:41.360
But, her only flaw is her sense of rhythm.

37:41.700 --> 37:44.370
Huh? But wasn't she able to play it just now?

37:44.370 --> 37:47.120
That's because the tempo was firmly set.

37:48.200 --> 37:52.120
It's more like I can't get the right groove...

37:52.750 --> 37:55.170
When playing with others, that is.

37:55.880 --> 37:59.920
And at EnCon, there won't be a conductor...

38:02.380 --> 38:03.800
I understand.

38:04.140 --> 38:08.020
Well, for now, let's give it another go?

38:08.020 --> 38:10.100
I'll play along as well.

38:10.100 --> 38:11.140
Sure...

38:14.690 --> 38:16.770
Okay, ready?

38:52.060 --> 38:53.980
Oh...

38:56.020 --> 38:57.110
Ah...

38:58.940 --> 39:01.360
What's wrong?

39:01.360 --> 39:02.700
Was it bad?

39:03.110 --> 39:05.490
Tsubame. Your breath.

39:05.910 --> 39:06.870
My breath?

39:06.870 --> 39:07.950
Breath?

39:07.950 --> 39:09.120
Breath?

39:09.580 --> 39:13.460
Yeah. Playing the marimba doesn't require air,

39:13.460 --> 39:15.790
so you might not be aware of it,

39:15.790 --> 39:19.550
but everyone else needs to take a breath to play.

39:20.090 --> 39:24.720
Tsubame looked like she wasn't breathing at all.

39:24.720 --> 39:27.220
Oh! No way she's not.

39:27.220 --> 39:28.430
Ah.

39:28.430 --> 39:29.970
No way! Seriously?!

39:29.970 --> 39:32.470
That never occurred to me.

39:32.470 --> 39:36.400
It's the same for percussion. They need to breathe together as well.

39:36.400 --> 39:38.310
How have you been doing it up till now?

39:38.810 --> 39:42.570
Listening and timing it by ear...

39:43.030 --> 39:45.950
It's not a rhythm game.

39:46.280 --> 39:48.990
You have to watch the others for it to work!

39:48.990 --> 39:52.240
Stuff like that does happen from time to time.

39:52.240 --> 39:54.410
I get it from some people too:

39:54.870 --> 39:57.880
"You didn't even know that?".

39:59.670 --> 40:02.340
Even if it's obvious to you,

40:02.340 --> 40:06.590
it might not be the same for others.

40:07.180 --> 40:09.090
Mm.

40:09.800 --> 40:14.100
<i>After that, Tsubame's performance began to show clarity and balance.</i>

40:15.100 --> 40:17.190
<i>Breathing together.</i>

40:17.190 --> 40:20.860
<i>A minor detail, but it was a eureka moment.</i>

40:20.860 --> 40:23.820
<i>In addition to the improvement in technical skills,</i>

40:23.820 --> 40:28.110
<i>she seemed to gradually start playing with more confidence.</i>

40:28.860 --> 40:33.490
<i>Hazuki's tuba playing was changing as well.</i>

40:34.450 --> 40:37.370
Hazuki, you've getting better, haven't you?

40:37.750 --> 40:39.170
Heh? Really?

40:39.170 --> 40:43.590
Yes, the sustained notes feel more solid.

40:44.050 --> 40:47.340
And your sound has become more consistent.

40:48.380 --> 40:50.590
It's a little frustrating.

40:50.590 --> 40:51.800
What?

40:51.800 --> 40:55.600
They all suddenly improved right after your practice.

40:56.060 --> 40:58.690
It's all due to their own efforts.

40:58.690 --> 41:00.060
Aren't we humble?

41:00.600 --> 41:04.320
But you really are suited for being club president.

41:05.110 --> 41:07.070
I don't know if that's true.

41:08.070 --> 41:12.870
But when you say it Reina, it makes me happy.

41:17.580 --> 41:20.460
<i>And thus, the day of the concert finally arrived.</i>

41:20.870 --> 41:24.420
Team Kousaka does it again!

41:24.880 --> 41:26.590
Oh, Kanade.

41:26.590 --> 41:29.510
I was listening to your performance earlier and thought,

41:29.510 --> 41:31.720
"I can't lose this."

41:32.090 --> 41:35.310
So we're called "Team Kousaka"?

41:36.020 --> 41:39.600
Then Kanade, wouldn't your team be "Team Hisaishi"?

41:39.600 --> 41:42.770
No, no. We don't have someone at the top.

41:42.770 --> 41:45.440
I guess you could say we are "Team Pacifist".

41:45.440 --> 41:49.110
If you put it like that, it actually does seem so.

41:50.030 --> 41:52.450
Performances in small groups like this...

41:52.450 --> 41:55.910
It's fascinating when people you don't expect turn out to be skilled, right?

41:55.910 --> 41:58.750
Yeah, that's what I thought as well.

41:59.200 --> 42:05.670
It also makes it easier for Taki-sensei to choose pieces for the free choice slot.

42:05.670 --> 42:09.380
The free choice repertoire for next year's competition?

42:09.380 --> 42:10.670
That's right.

42:11.130 --> 42:16.100
It would be a shame if we didn't choose a piece highlighting our talents.

42:19.390 --> 42:22.520
I've just been looking forward to having fun in the ensemble.

42:22.520 --> 42:25.480
Would that be a lack of awareness as club president?

42:28.820 --> 42:31.530
Isn't that the correct thing to look forward to?

42:37.330 --> 42:39.240
You're unusually kind today.

42:42.750 --> 42:45.420
I'm always kind, you know.

42:47.040 --> 42:48.750
Are you okay on that side?

42:48.750 --> 42:49.760
Yup.

42:49.760 --> 42:51.760
We're almost at the step.

42:53.720 --> 42:58.010
The marimba is expensive. We have to be careful not to damage it.

42:58.600 --> 43:00.020
Let's do it?

43:00.020 --> 43:01.100
Yes.

43:01.100 --> 43:02.270
There... we go.

43:28.290 --> 43:29.920
President Oumae.

43:30.960 --> 43:34.930
You've been on the competition team since first year, right?

43:34.930 --> 43:36.090
Yes.

43:41.770 --> 43:44.980
Is playing in a real competition scary?

43:44.980 --> 43:48.610
I wouldn't say it's scary... but I do get nervous.

43:48.610 --> 43:50.230
I see.

43:51.190 --> 43:52.730
And, lift!

44:02.740 --> 44:04.160
Ready... up!

44:06.580 --> 44:08.750
You know...

44:09.750 --> 44:12.250
I've never been very skilled.

44:12.250 --> 44:17.380
So I've always taken for granted that I wouldn't be a competition member.

44:18.220 --> 44:19.640
But...

44:20.550 --> 44:24.640
Right now, is it okay for me to want to participate too?

44:29.610 --> 44:32.440
There's no one stopping you.

44:32.440 --> 44:33.780
You think so?

44:34.400 --> 44:35.570
Of course not.

44:38.070 --> 44:39.490
I see.

44:56.670 --> 44:59.010
<i>Whether I'm a good president,</i>

44:59.010 --> 45:01.090
<i>I'm uncertain.</i>

45:01.090 --> 45:07.270
<i>But spurred by Tsubame's change of heart,
feelings of bliss grow within me.</i>

45:26.370 --> 45:30.170
We've practiced as a group for quite some time.

45:30.170 --> 45:35.800
Today, we're finally able to show off our hard work.

45:35.800 --> 45:40.010
Let's win this qualifier, and advance to the contest.

45:54.270 --> 45:55.320
Kumiko.

45:56.110 --> 45:57.030
Yes!

45:58.240 --> 46:00.030
Kitauji fight!

