50:22.120 --> 50:25.460
A few days later

50:26.000 --> 50:27.840
Want a bite?

50:27.840 --> 50:29.840
Are chocolate buns good?

50:29.840 --> 50:32.010
I can't guarantee anything...

50:32.010 --> 50:34.800
You're just using me as a guinea pig, aren't you?

50:34.800 --> 50:37.890
Ugh, why did you even buy that?

50:39.470 --> 50:40.640
Ah...

50:40.640 --> 50:41.640
Hmm?

50:45.360 --> 50:46.400
S-sweet!

50:46.400 --> 50:47.480
Told you!

50:49.320 --> 50:53.910
I should have bought a steamed bun too.

50:53.910 --> 50:55.910
I'll give you a chocolate bun if you'd like.

50:55.910 --> 50:59.370
Oh! You're a god, Kousaka!

50:59.370 --> 51:02.710
Me too! Please give some to Midori too, Goddess!

51:04.120 --> 51:08.210
The members should be returning from the venue by now.

51:09.300 --> 51:13.720
It seems like the clarinets made it to the Kansai competition.

51:13.720 --> 51:18.310
Indeed... Hearing that makes me regret it again.

51:18.310 --> 51:21.470
It can't be helped, they were good.

51:22.230 --> 51:26.100
But you know, we did win the general vote.

51:26.100 --> 51:28.820
Well, that's just a popularity vote.

51:28.820 --> 51:31.360
Midori's group came in third.

51:31.360 --> 51:35.320
I'm sure the one most frustrated is Hisaishi.

51:35.320 --> 51:38.830
They came in second in both the members and public vote.

51:39.200 --> 51:44.290
She was so aggravated.
Where did the pacifism go, Kanade?

51:44.290 --> 51:47.290
But we can go for it next time.

51:48.920 --> 51:50.800
Together.

51:51.380 --> 51:52.670
Next time...

51:53.800 --> 51:55.300
The Brass Band Competition.

52:01.600 --> 52:04.520
It'll be our last competition, right?

52:04.520 --> 52:05.560
Right.

52:06.270 --> 52:09.440
We'll win, won't we? Gold at nationals?

52:11.190 --> 52:12.280
Yeah.

52:16.490 --> 52:21.200
And so, the next piece begins.
